00:52:30.000 --> 00:52:32.999
E.V.. track physical anomalies.

815
00:52:33.000 --> 00:52:35.999
Searching for physical
anomalies between subjects.

816
00:52:36.000 --> 00:52:38.000
Please stand by.

817
00:52:42.000 --> 00:52:45.000
Thank you all so much for coming today.

818
00:52:51.000 --> 00:52:52.999
I'm sorry about that.

819
00:52:53.000 --> 00:52:54.999
Give it up for Spider-Man.

820
00:52:55.000 --> 00:52:58.000
It race for the love of his
life. and it's not looking good.

821
00:52:59.000 --> 00:53:02.999
Come on. Spidey. Keep up.

822
00:53:03.000 --> 00:53:04.000
Excuse me.

823
00:53:04.000 --> 00:53:05.000
Sorry.

824
00:53:18.000 --> 00:53:21.000
E.V.. run these numbers with the others.

825
00:53:23.000 --> 00:53:26.000
Analysing jump distances from patterns.

826
00:53:28.000 --> 00:53:29.999
Get in the jump data.

827
00:53:30.000 --> 00:53:32.000
Calculating.

828
00:53:35.000 --> 00:53:37.999
Come on. I need an answer.

829
00:53:38.000 --> 00:53:40.000
Calculations complete.

830
00:53:55.000 --> 00:53:57.000
You have a limit to your
job radius. don't you?

831
00:53:58.000 --> 00:53:59.999
33 feet.

832
00:54:00.000 --> 00:54:02.999
I don't see anybody up
here for you to hop into.

833
00:54:03.000 --> 00:54:04.999
Very clever.

834
00:54:05.000 --> 00:54:09.000
Like I said. you're not getting near her.

835
00:54:24.000 --> 00:54:25.999
I'm sorry but you're in danger.
Where's your roommate?

836
00:54:26.000 --> 00:54:27.999
- What?
- Where is Ned?

837
00:54:28.000 --> 00:54:29.000
In Boss with friends. Why?

838
00:54:29.001 --> 00:54:30.999
You've got to come with me.

839
00:54:31.000 --> 00:54:32.999
I don't know if you're the real Spider-Man.
I'm not coming with you.

840
00:54:33.000 --> 00:54:34.999
We don't have time for
this. Please come on.

841
00:54:35.000 --> 00:54:36.999
You need to get out of my apartment.

842
00:54:37.000 --> 00:54:39.999
This is going to sound insane but there is someone
who is after you who is really dangerous. okay?

843
00:54:40.000 --> 00:54:42.999
I promised you that I would keep you safe.

844
00:54:43.000 --> 00:54:46.000
Please. you just have to trust me. Come on.

845
00:54:48.000 --> 00:54:50.000
Fine.

846
00:54:56.000 --> 00:54:58.000
Web. Stop.

847
00:55:00.000 --> 00:55:02.000
Web. Stop.

848
00:55:05.000 --> 00:55:07.000
Web. Stop.

849
00:55:12.000 --> 00:55:13.999
- Are you okay?
- Yeah. yeah. I'm fine.

850
00:55:14.000 --> 00:55:15.999
Okay. we should be safe up here.

851
00:55:16.000 --> 00:55:17.999
Okay. safe from what?

852
00:55:18.000 --> 00:55:19.999
Uh. I'm not entirely sure.

853
00:55:20.000 --> 00:55:21.999
Okay. well. what do they want with me?

854
00:55:22.000 --> 00:55:23.999
- I don't know.
- You don't know?

855
00:55:24.000 --> 00:55:26.999
It doesn't make any sense.
Why would they choose me?

856
00:55:27.000 --> 00:55:29.999
Well. I wish I could tell you.

857
00:55:30.000 --> 00:55:35.000
We knew each other. didn't we?

858
00:55:38.000 --> 00:55:39.999
What?

859
00:55:40.000 --> 00:55:41.999
It's the only explanation.

860
00:55:42.000 --> 00:55:46.999
It's been driving me crazy for years all the
times that Spider-Man saved either me or Ned.

861
00:55:47.000 --> 00:55:51.000
It was the Washington Monument and then it
was London and Prague and the Night Monkey.

862
00:55:52.000 --> 00:55:55.000
I mean. twice is a coincidence
but over and over again..

863
00:55:57.000 --> 00:56:00.000
We knew each other. Tell me I'm wrong.

864
00:56:01.000 --> 00:56:02.000
Well. you're wrong.

865
00:56:02.001 --> 00:56:04.999
Well. were we were we classmates
or our friends or something?

866
00:56:05.000 --> 00:56:07.999
I don't know what you're talking about.

867
00:56:08.000 --> 00:56:10.999
Were we something more?

868
00:56:11.000 --> 00:56:15.000
I just. I can't remember and I feel
like someone scrambled my brain..

869
00:56:15.001 --> 00:56:17.999
And you're the only one who would know why.

870
00:56:18.000 --> 00:56:19.999
This is crazy.

871
00:56:20.000 --> 00:56:23.000
I know that you can't tell me the truth.

872
00:56:24.000 --> 00:56:27.000
But I need to know.

873
00:56:31.000 --> 00:56:35.000
Maybe there's a part of
me that still remembers.

874
00:57:13.000 --> 00:57:18.000
- Peter.
- MJ

875
00:57:25.000 --> 00:57:27.000
I've missed you so much.

876
00:57:32.000 --> 00:57:33.999
I can't believe you figured it out.

877
00:57:34.000 --> 00:57:35.000
I did.

878
00:57:41.000 --> 00:57:42.000
Go ahead. Peter.

879
00:57:43.000 --> 00:57:44.000
Touch her.

880
00:57:45.000 --> 00:57:46.000
Hold her.

881
00:57:47.000 --> 00:57:49.000
You've been wanting to do this for so long.

882
00:57:57.000 --> 00:58:02.000
True Love Kiss breaks his spell
and reunites to star-crossed lovers.

883
00:58:04.000 --> 00:58:05.000
MJ would vomit.

884
00:58:08.000 --> 00:58:10.000
You really are a simple spider. aren't you?

885
00:58:13.000 --> 00:58:14.999
I see why you like her.

886
00:58:15.000 --> 00:58:16.000
She's a...

887
00:58:17.000 --> 00:58:18.000
She's smart.

888
00:58:19.000 --> 00:58:20.000
Funny.

889
00:58:21.000 --> 00:58:23.000
And a little dark and twisted.

890
00:58:26.000 --> 00:58:27.999
I mean. it is sad.

891
00:58:28.000 --> 00:58:32.000
There is like no thoughts of you in here.

892
00:58:33.000 --> 00:58:34.000
Once or ever.

893
00:58:35.000 --> 00:58:37.000
But you knew that didn't you?

894
00:58:38.000 --> 00:58:40.000
You're a monster.

895
00:58:41.000 --> 00:58:42.999
If you loved someone
the way that I loved her.

896
00:58:43.000 --> 00:58:45.999
you'd know that what you're
doing right now is unforgivable.

897
00:58:46.000 --> 00:58:47.000
Oh. is that so?

898
00:58:54.000 --> 00:58:57.040
You know. some people would kill to
hold the person they love one last time.

899
00:58:59.000 --> 00:59:00.000
Stop it. now.

900
00:59:09.000 --> 00:59:11.000
You're running out of time. Peter.

901
00:59:12.000 --> 00:59:16.000
Soon enough. it won't just be your friends
who don't remember you're Peter Parker.

902
00:59:17.000 --> 00:59:19.000
Maybe you should
write a letter to yourself.

903
00:59:23.000 --> 00:59:24.000
Get out of her.

904
00:59:26.000 --> 00:59:27.160
Who's the monster now. Peter?

905
00:59:42.000 --> 00:59:43.000
What?

906
00:59:52.000 --> 00:59:54.999
MJ. No. no. no. Oh God.

907
00:59:55.000 --> 00:59:56.000
Oh God. please.

908
00:59:56.000 --> 00:59:57.000
Now. come on.

909
00:59:57.000 --> 00:59:58.000
Come on. come on. come on.

910
00:59:58.001 --> 01:00:00.999
Oh. thank God. thank God.

911
01:00:01.000 --> 01:00:01.999
Oh. you're okay.

912
01:00:02.000 --> 01:00:03.000
Well. you're okay.

913
01:00:04.000 --> 01:00:05.000
Oh. I'm so sorry.

914
01:00:07.000 --> 01:00:08.000
Stop.

915
01:00:08.000 --> 01:00:09.000
Well. please stop.

916
01:00:09.000 --> 01:00:10.000
Please. don't quit.

917
01:00:10.000 --> 01:00:11.000
You win. you win. you win.

918
01:00:11.000 --> 01:00:12.000
You win. you win.

919
01:00:12.000 --> 01:00:13.000
Just don't hurt her.

920
01:00:15.000 --> 01:00:17.000
You're a mess. Spider-Man.

921
01:00:19.000 --> 01:00:20.999
Anytime I want.

922
01:00:21.000 --> 01:00:23.000
I can be anyone I want.

923
01:00:24.000 --> 01:00:26.000
So you can't protect MJ..

924
01:00:27.000 --> 01:00:28.000
Even from yourself.

925
01:00:36.000 --> 01:00:37.999
It really is a nice letter.

926
01:00:38.000 --> 01:00:39.000
Little heavy-handed.

927
01:00:39.000 --> 01:00:40.000
But not bad.

928
01:00:59.000 --> 01:01:00.000
You're okay.

929
01:01:00.001 --> 01:01:01.999
I'm going to take you someplace safe.

930
01:01:02.000 --> 01:01:03.000
Come on.

931
01:01:04.000 --> 01:01:05.999
Take me to 3165 Live Island Street.

932
01:01:06.000 --> 01:01:09.000
Navigating to the Empire State University.

933
01:01:18.000 --> 01:01:19.000
I got you. I got you.

934
01:01:19.000 --> 01:01:20.000
- Are you sure?
- Yup

935
01:01:20.001 --> 01:01:23.001
- Cause I feel like I'm slipping a little bit.
- You're not slipping. - Okay

936
01:01:24.000 --> 01:01:28.000
- You're okay.
- I'm fine. I'm fine. I'm fine.

937
01:01:32.000 --> 01:01:34.999
- Can we just slow down for like two seconds?
- Well. we're almost there.

938
01:01:35.000 --> 01:01:36.999
Yeah. yeah. but you just
told me I was mind controlled.

939
01:01:37.000 --> 01:01:38.000
Well. not technically.

940
01:01:38.001 --> 01:01:39.999
I mean. you're lucky I
believe in that stuff. okay?

941
01:01:40.000 --> 01:01:41.999
Because governments have been
doing it for years. especially the French.

942
01:01:42.000 --> 01:01:43.000
Are you okay?

943
01:01:43.000 --> 01:01:44.000
Yeah. look. sorry.

944
01:01:44.001 --> 01:01:46.000
I'm just trying to take you
someplace safe. okay?

945
01:01:51.000 --> 01:01:52.000
I don't feel safe.

946
01:02:06.000 --> 01:02:07.000
Ah.

947
01:02:10.000 --> 01:02:11.999
You're losing it. kid.

948
01:02:12.000 --> 01:02:13.999
I thought you'd be able to
see that coming a mile away.

949
01:02:14.000 --> 01:02:15.000
What is wrong with you?

950
01:02:15.000 --> 01:02:16.000
You could've killed us.

951
01:02:16.000 --> 01:02:17.000
Excuse me?

952
01:02:17.001 --> 01:02:19.999
You show up to my house unannounced.
what you think is gonna happen?

953
01:02:20.000 --> 01:02:21.000
Wait. this is your house?

954
01:02:21.000 --> 01:02:22.000
Who the hell is that?

955
01:02:22.000 --> 01:02:23.000
Who the hell are you?

956
01:02:23.001 --> 01:02:25.000
She's um...

957
01:02:26.000 --> 01:02:27.000
You know?

958
01:02:27.000 --> 01:02:28.000
No. I don't know.

959
01:02:28.000 --> 01:02:29.000
It's why I just asked you.

960
01:02:29.001 --> 01:02:30.999
She's in danger. Frank.

961
01:02:31.000 --> 01:02:32.000
Look. I need your help. okay?

962
01:02:32.000 --> 01:02:33.000
Yeah. it looks like it.

963
01:02:33.000 --> 01:02:34.000
Well. come on. you owe me.

964
01:02:34.000 --> 01:02:35.000
Ah. come on.

965
01:02:35.000 --> 01:02:36.000
Aren't you sick of this story?

966
01:02:36.000 --> 01:02:37.000
Staten Island.

967
01:02:37.000 --> 01:02:38.000
Nah. that's not an island.

968
01:02:38.001 --> 01:02:39.999
What more do you want me to do?

969
01:02:40.000 --> 01:02:41.000
I literally saved your life.

970
01:02:41.000 --> 01:02:42.000
You're out of your mind. kid!

971
01:02:42.001 --> 01:02:45.999
- What. I gotta save it twice to get a favour out of you?
- That guy could've hit you with a handful of rice.

972
01:02:46.000 --> 01:02:47.000
I mean. what does that sound like to you?

973
01:02:47.001 --> 01:02:51.721
- I had him where I want him. I'm seeing him right there.
- A drug dealer was gonna shoot a guy. then I webbed the gun.

974
01:02:52.000 --> 01:02:53.000
Okay. fine. go ahead.

975
01:02:53.001 --> 01:02:54.321
What does that sound like to you?

976
01:02:56.000 --> 01:02:57.000
I don't care.

977
01:02:57.000 --> 01:02:58.000
I just want to go home.

978
01:02:58.000 --> 01:02:59.000
That's an excellent idea.

979
01:02:59.000 --> 01:03:00.000
Kick rocks. go away.

980
01:03:00.001 --> 01:03:02.000
No. wait. wait. wait.
wait. wait. Frank. wait.

981
01:03:03.000 --> 01:03:04.000
Please.

982
01:03:04.001 --> 01:03:05.999
Hey. I've got to keep her safe. okay?

983
01:03:06.000 --> 01:03:08.000
And I don't have anywhere else to go.

984
01:03:12.000 --> 01:03:13.000
You like chili?

985
01:03:14.000 --> 01:03:15.000
I made chili.

986
01:03:17.000 --> 01:03:18.000
All right. just...

987
01:03:19.000 --> 01:03:20.000
Watch out for the claymores.

988
01:03:20.001 --> 01:03:23.000
Don't want to pick up pieces
of you for the next two weeks.

989
01:03:24.000 --> 01:03:26.000
Hey. I definitely would not eat that chili.

990
01:03:28.000 --> 01:03:30.999
So you're telling me that maniac
that was behind all that tech nonsense

991
01:03:31.000 --> 01:03:32.999
is nothing but a goddamn teenager?

992
01:03:33.000 --> 01:03:34.000
And it's not just the tank.

993
01:03:34.001 --> 01:03:36.999
It's every attack on Damage
Control this past month.

994
01:03:37.000 --> 01:03:38.999
How does a kid learn how to drive a tank?

995
01:03:39.000 --> 01:03:40.000
I don't know. Frank.

996
01:03:40.001 --> 01:03:41.999
Beat you all over the street like that.

997
01:03:42.000 --> 01:03:43.000
She did not beat me.

998
01:03:44.000 --> 01:03:45.000
Is this your family?

999
01:03:48.000 --> 01:03:50.000
Would you get the hell away from that?

1000
01:03:51.000 --> 01:03:52.999
Look. I got one rule in this house.

1001
01:03:53.000 --> 01:03:54.000
You don't touch anything.

1002
01:03:54.001 --> 01:03:55.999
You don't move anything.

1003
01:03:56.000 --> 01:03:59.000
You sure as shit don't has many
goddamn questions about anything.

1004
01:04:01.000 --> 01:04:02.000
So three rules.

1005
01:04:05.000 --> 01:04:06.999
Is see why you like her.

1006
01:04:07.000 --> 01:04:09.000
You can go put some pants on.

1007
01:04:10.000 --> 01:04:12.000
Don't touch the chili.

1008
01:04:13.000 --> 01:04:14.000
I like him.

1009
01:04:16.000 --> 01:04:17.000
What was she doing?

1010
01:04:18.000 --> 01:04:19.999
So I managed to pull
those image from my fight

1011
01:04:20.000 --> 01:04:22.000
and then run them through system.

1012
01:04:25.000 --> 01:04:26.000
Who is she?

1013
01:04:26.000 --> 01:04:27.000
Until a couple of months ago?

1014
01:04:27.000 --> 01:04:28.000
Nobody.

1015
01:04:29.000 --> 01:04:30.999
She was in and out of foster care.

1016
01:04:31.000 --> 01:04:32.000
psych hospitals.

1017
01:04:32.001 --> 01:04:33.999
and then eventually she ran
away and dropped off the grid.

1018
01:04:34.000 --> 01:04:35.000
There's hardly any information about her.

1019
01:04:35.000 --> 01:04:36.000
There hasn't been scrubbed.

1020
01:04:36.001 --> 01:04:37.999
but she's classified as a telepath.

1021
01:04:38.000 --> 01:04:40.000
And now we have a name.

1022
01:04:43.000 --> 01:04:44.000
Jean Gray.

1023
01:04:46.000 --> 01:04:47.000
Yeah.

1024
01:04:47.001 --> 01:04:49.999
These are the Damage Control
sites that she hasn't hit yet.

1025
01:04:50.000 --> 01:04:51.999
So if she surfaces.

1026
01:04:52.000 --> 01:04:54.000
then my facial tracking
program will pick her up.

1027
01:04:55.000 --> 01:04:56.000
Right.

1028
01:04:56.001 --> 01:04:58.000
Oh yeah? What then?

1029
01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:02.999
Well. don't worry about "what then."
Just look after her.

1030
01:05:03.000 --> 01:05:04.000
Don't worry about it. huh?

1031
01:05:04.001 --> 01:05:05.999
I'm just supposed to sit here
and babysit your girlfriend?

1032
01:05:06.000 --> 01:05:07.999
I don't need to be babysat. so yeah
She's not my girlfriend.

1033
01:05:08.000 --> 01:05:09.000
All right. all right.

1034
01:05:09.000 --> 01:05:10.000
Look. what's the plan. huh?

1035
01:05:10.001 --> 01:05:13.999
Just gotta hope that your
facial tracking program works?

1036
01:05:14.000 --> 01:05:15.999
And you get yourself killed.
I gotta watch her the rest of my life?

1037
01:05:16.000 --> 01:05:17.999
I'm not going to get killed. Frank.

1038
01:05:18.000 --> 01:05:19.000
I can catch her. okay?

1039
01:05:19.001 --> 01:05:20.999
I just have to fix my inhibitor

1040
01:05:21.000 --> 01:05:22.120
and then I'll be good to go.

1041
01:05:23.000 --> 01:05:24.360
Well. what do you need to do that?

1042
01:05:26.000 --> 01:05:27.000
Frank.

1043
01:05:27.001 --> 01:05:29.000
You do not have what
I need to do that. okay?

1044
01:05:31.000 --> 01:05:32.000
You know you've got some mouth on you.

1045
01:05:32.001 --> 01:05:33.999
What do you think you
have an anti-static mat...?

1046
01:05:34.000 --> 01:05:35.999
A tonal probe and a micro tools?

1047
01:05:36.000 --> 01:05:38.000
I got all that shit.

1048
01:05:39.000 --> 01:05:40.000
What for?

1049
01:05:40.000 --> 01:05:41.000
Bombs.

1050
01:05:41.000 --> 01:05:42.000
Bingo.

1051
01:05:44.000 --> 01:05:45.000
Unbelievable.

1052
01:05:57.000 --> 01:05:58.999
Hey. do you think it's safe
to maybe call someone

1053
01:05:59.000 --> 01:06:00.080
and let them know I'm okay?

1054
01:06:05.000 --> 01:06:06.000
Like your boyfriend?

1055
01:06:07.000 --> 01:06:08.000
No.

1056
01:06:08.000 --> 01:06:09.000
Like my roommate.

1057
01:06:10.000 --> 01:06:11.000
Oh.

1058
01:06:13.000 --> 01:06:14.999
I don't think that's such
a good idea. you know?

1059
01:06:15.000 --> 01:06:17.999
Because she already knows who he is

1060
01:06:18.000 --> 01:06:19.999
and she can inhabit anyone she wants.

1061
01:06:20.000 --> 01:06:21.000
All right. Yeah.

1062
01:06:21.000 --> 01:06:22.000
Yeah.

1063
01:06:22.000 --> 01:06:23.000
You're right.

1064
01:06:23.000 --> 01:06:24.000
Sorry.

1065
01:06:24.000 --> 01:06:25.000
No. it's fine.

1066
01:06:25.000 --> 01:06:26.000
I totally get it.

1067
01:06:28.000 --> 01:06:29.040
If I called my boyfriend..

1068
01:06:30.000 --> 01:06:31.999
He'd just ask me a bunch of
questions that I couldn't answer..

1069
01:06:32.000 --> 01:06:35.999
And he'd tell me I was
being withholding again.

1070
01:06:36.000 --> 01:06:37.000
Withholding?

1071
01:06:37.000 --> 01:06:38.000
Yep.

1072
01:06:38.001 --> 01:06:40.000
Sounds like your
boyfriend's kind of a jerk.

1073
01:06:42.000 --> 01:06:43.999
But why would he think you're withholding?

1074
01:06:44.000 --> 01:06:48.000
I don't know. You tell me.
masked vigilante behind the curtain.

1075
01:06:49.000 --> 01:06:50.000
