she tried to say something.

1344
01:25:40.500 --> 01:25:42.499
A name: Sara.

1345
01:25:42.500 --> 01:25:44.499
Does that mean something to you?

1346
01:25:44.500 --> 01:25:46.499
Before you got the inhibitor on her.

1347
01:25:46.500 --> 01:25:48.499
she managed to get to my mind for a moment.

1348
01:25:48.500 --> 01:25:54.499
Sara was the name of someone I
worked closely with that recently passed.

1349
01:25:54.500 --> 01:25:58.499
I'm sorry to hear that.

1350
01:25:58.500 --> 01:26:02.500
Somehow the memory of
Sara must have affected her.

1351
01:26:04.500 --> 01:26:08.499
Well. I'd love to talk to her when
she wakes up. if that's all right.

1352
01:26:08.500 --> 01:26:12.499
Of course. she'll be transferred
to our facility in Roosevelt Island.

1353
01:26:12.500 --> 01:26:14.499
I'm just as eager to get
her talking as you are.

1354
01:26:14.500 --> 01:26:16.499
but let's not strain her
too much in one day.

1355
01:26:16.500 --> 01:26:18.499
Yeah. of course.

1356
01:26:18.500 --> 01:26:20.499
Thank you. Spider-Man.

1357
01:26:20.500 --> 01:26:22.500
My pleasure.

1358
01:26:26.500 --> 01:26:28.500
Okay.

1359
01:26:36.000 --> 01:26:37.499
MJ. it worked. She's in custody.

1360
01:26:37.500 --> 01:26:38.500
You're safe now.

1361
01:26:41.500 --> 01:26:43.500
You left this?

1362
01:26:50.500 --> 01:26:52.499
Did you want me to find it?

1363
01:26:52.500 --> 01:26:54.499
No.

1364
01:26:54.500 --> 01:26:56.499
No. no.

1365
01:26:56.500 --> 01:26:58.499
Look. I can explain. okay?

1366
01:26:58.500 --> 01:27:00.500
Can you take that off. please?

1367
01:27:02.500 --> 01:27:04.499
What?

1368
01:27:04.500 --> 01:27:06.499
The mask.

1369
01:27:06.500 --> 01:27:12.500
I think I deserve to have this
conversation with "Peter Parker".

1370
01:27:36.500 --> 01:27:40.500
You came to the party at
our apartment the other night.

1371
01:27:44.500 --> 01:27:48.499
And the donut shop.

1372
01:27:48.500 --> 01:27:52.499
The year I went off to school.

1373
01:27:52.500 --> 01:27:54.499
Why didn't you tell me then?

1374
01:27:54.500 --> 01:27:56.499
I was trying to protect you.

1375
01:27:56.500 --> 01:28:00.499
I've almost been killed like.
five times the past 24 hours..

1376
01:28:00.500 --> 01:28:02.499
So it's not really working that well.

1377
01:28:02.500 --> 01:28:04.499
I know. I'm sorry. I..

1378
01:28:04.500 --> 01:28:08.500
Were you ever going to tell me?

1379
01:28:12.500 --> 01:28:16.499
Right.

1380
01:28:16.500 --> 01:28:18.499
So you're just going to
make that decision for me?

1381
01:28:18.500 --> 01:28:20.499
I know. I'm sorry.

1382
01:28:20.500 --> 01:28:22.499
I don't really need you to
keep saying that you're sorry.

1383
01:28:22.500 --> 01:28:24.499
I don't know what you want me to tell you.

1384
01:28:24.500 --> 01:28:26.500
I want you to tell me why
you would do this to me.

1385
01:28:32.500 --> 01:28:34.500
I lost someone.

1386
01:28:36.500 --> 01:28:40.500
And they'd still be
here if it wasn't for me.

1387
01:28:44.500 --> 01:28:46.499
I didn't read you that letter because..

1388
01:28:46.500 --> 01:28:48.499
I didn't want anything
like that to happen to you.

1389
01:28:48.500 --> 01:28:50.499
That's not really your decision.

1390
01:28:50.500 --> 01:28:52.500
I know it's not. but..

1391
01:28:54.500 --> 01:28:56.500
You mean everything to me.

1392
01:28:58.500 --> 01:29:02.499
And I've been trying to
live my life without you. but..

1393
01:29:02.500 --> 01:29:04.500
I can't.

1394
01:29:10.500 --> 01:29:12.500
I love you.

1395
01:29:18.500 --> 01:29:26.500
This spell or whatever it is that you did..

1396
01:29:30.500 --> 01:29:32.500
It worked.

1397
01:29:34.500 --> 01:29:36.499
All these memories that you're
saying that we have together.

1398
01:29:36.500 --> 01:29:38.499
I don't..

1399
01:29:38.500 --> 01:29:40.500
I don't have them.

1400
01:29:44.500 --> 01:29:46.499
And I do see why. you know.

1401
01:29:46.500 --> 01:29:48.499
and she would love. the girl you..

1402
01:29:48.500 --> 01:29:50.500
Wrote that letter to. but..

1403
01:29:54.500 --> 01:29:56.499
I understand..

1404
01:29:56.500 --> 01:30:00.500
That you did what you
had to do to protect her.

1405
01:30:02.500 --> 01:30:04.500
And for that. I'm so grateful.

1406
01:30:08.500 --> 01:30:10.500
But I..

1407
01:30:12.500 --> 01:30:14.500
I don't love you.

1408
01:30:16.500 --> 01:30:20.500
You said I don't. I don't even know you.

1409
01:30:30.500 --> 01:30:32.500
I should probably go now.

1410
01:30:38.500 --> 01:30:40.500
I really am sorry. Peter.

1411
01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:06.000
I don't have a phone. Do
you mind taking me home?

1412
01:31:08.000 --> 01:31:09.000
Yeah. of course.

1413
01:31:09.001 --> 01:31:11.000
Thank you.

1414
01:31:53.000 --> 01:31:54.000
Thank you.

1415
01:31:54.000 --> 01:31:55.000
Yeah. sure.

1416
01:31:55.001 --> 01:31:56.999
I'm gonna...

1417
01:31:57.000 --> 01:31:59.000
Oh. yeah. Yeah. of course.

1418
01:32:08.000 --> 01:32:09.000
Do you want to come up?

1419
01:32:11.000 --> 01:32:13.000
Just to say hi to Ned. maybe?

1420
01:32:17.000 --> 01:32:18.000
I would love that.

1421
01:32:20.000 --> 01:32:25.999
The Hulk. aka Dr. Bruce Banner. is in custody.
currently being transferred to a psychiatric ward.

1422
01:32:26.000 --> 01:32:27.000
Oh. so sad.

1423
01:32:27.001 --> 01:32:34.000
After years as a peaceful academic. the question
the world asked today is. "what happened?"

1424
01:32:40.000 --> 01:32:41.999
Hey. I'm nearby.

1425
01:32:42.000 --> 01:32:43.000
Hey. I'm nearby.

1426
01:32:43.000 --> 01:32:44.000
And then?

1427
01:32:44.000 --> 01:32:45.000
Yeah.

1428
01:32:45.000 --> 01:32:46.000
Hey. I'm nearby.

1429
01:32:46.000 --> 01:32:47.000
Huh.

1430
01:32:47.001 --> 01:32:48.999
You're not gonna believe this.

1431
01:32:49.000 --> 01:32:53.999
But the Spidey-tracker app says
that Spider-Man is in the direct vicinity.

1432
01:32:54.000 --> 01:32:55.000
Oh. yeah?

1433
01:32:55.000 --> 01:32:56.000
No way. that's crazy.

1434
01:32:58.000 --> 01:32:59.000
Uh. Ned?

1435
01:32:59.000 --> 01:33:00.000
Spider-Man?

1436
01:33:00.000 --> 01:33:01.000
Spider-Man. Ned?

1437
01:33:01.001 --> 01:33:02.999
It's nice to meet you. Ned.

1438
01:33:03.000 --> 01:33:04.000
Hello.

1439
01:33:04.001 --> 01:33:05.999
I'm not like a weirdo for anything.

1440
01:33:06.000 --> 01:33:07.000
He's a little weird.

1441
01:33:07.000 --> 01:33:08.000
Why?

1442
01:33:08.000 --> 01:33:09.000
Why are you here?

1443
01:33:09.001 --> 01:33:10.999
Oh. I...

1444
01:33:11.000 --> 01:33:12.999
I was on the subway.

1445
01:33:13.000 --> 01:33:14.000
Platform. right.

1446
01:33:14.000 --> 01:33:15.000
And she's on her phone.

1447
01:33:15.001 --> 01:33:16.999
Yeah. I double distracted
and the train was coming.

1448
01:33:17.000 --> 01:33:18.999
And I just swooped her right up.

1449
01:33:19.000 --> 01:33:21.000
Yeah. saved the day.

1450
01:33:22.000 --> 01:33:23.999
Oh. my God.

1451
01:33:24.000 --> 01:33:25.999
Why has that never happened to me?

1452
01:33:26.000 --> 01:33:29.999
So. what if you're a mid-swing
and you decide you need a pee?

1453
01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:31.999
Do you just land on top of a building?

1454
01:33:32.000 --> 01:33:33.000
What?

1455
01:33:33.001 --> 01:33:34.999
Do you drop down the ground
level and run into a coffee shop?

1456
01:33:35.000 --> 01:33:36.000
You're like. hey. Spider-Man. I need a pee.

1457
01:33:36.001 --> 01:33:37.999
Or do you find a rooftop somewhere?

1458
01:33:38.000 --> 01:33:39.999
No. I don't find a rooftop somewhere. Ned.

1459
01:33:40.000 --> 01:33:41.999
Is this really what you want
to be asking him right now?

1460
01:33:42.000 --> 01:33:43.000
Yeah. dude. come on.

1461
01:33:43.000 --> 01:33:44.000
You can ask me anything.

1462
01:33:44.000 --> 01:33:45.000
You want to know how my web shoiters work?

1463
01:33:45.001 --> 01:33:46.999
I mean. I already know
how the web shooters work.

1464
01:33:47.000 --> 01:33:48.000
Is that right?

1465
01:33:48.001 --> 01:33:50.999
Well. there's obviously some
sort of sheer thinning fluid

1466
01:33:51.000 --> 01:33:53.999
that is cycling within a chamber. right?

1467
01:33:54.000 --> 01:33:55.000
So you can keep this liquid form.

1468
01:33:55.001 --> 01:33:56.999
And then when you activate
it by pressing on the triggers.

1469
01:33:57.000 --> 01:33:58.999
it runs through a Teflon turbine.

1470
01:33:59.000 --> 01:34:01.999
And then it hardens when
it interacts with the air.

1471
01:34:02.000 --> 01:34:03.000
Right?

1472
01:34:06.000 --> 01:34:07.999
I mean. not exactly. but...

1473
01:34:08.000 --> 01:34:09.000
Okay. okay.

1474
01:34:09.000 --> 01:34:10.000
Well. then tell me what's in the web fluid.

1475
01:34:10.001 --> 01:34:12.999
I would guess something
like a long chain polymer.

1476
01:34:13.000 --> 01:34:14.000
A nylon?

1477
01:34:14.000 --> 01:34:15.000
That's pretty close.

1478
01:34:15.000 --> 01:34:16.000
Okay. okay.

1479
01:34:16.001 --> 01:34:17.999
What about Romax or...

1480
01:34:18.000 --> 01:34:19.000
Or. Kevlar!

1481
01:34:21.000 --> 01:34:22.999
"All right then. keep your secrets."

1482
01:34:23.000 --> 01:34:24.999
"If you are referring to the
indicident with the dragon..

1483
01:34:25.000 --> 01:34:26.999
I was very much involved."

1484
01:34:27.000 --> 01:34:32.000
"All I did was simply give your uncle
a little nudge out the door."

1485
01:34:34.000 --> 01:34:35.000
Solid reference.

1486
01:34:36.000 --> 01:34:37.999
Ooh. Banh Mi time.

1487
01:34:38.000 --> 01:34:39.000
You ordered Banh Mi's?

1488
01:34:39.000 --> 01:34:40.000
I ordered five Banh Mi's.

1489
01:34:40.001 --> 01:34:41.999
We have Spider-Man in the apartment.

1490
01:34:42.000 --> 01:34:43.000
He's going to get fed.

1491
01:34:46.000 --> 01:34:47.000
Sorry about him.

1492
01:34:47.001 --> 01:34:48.999
He's just like very
excited that you're here.

1493
01:34:49.000 --> 01:34:50.000
Are you kidding?

1494
01:34:50.001 --> 01:34:51.999
It's like the most fun I've had in years.

1495
01:34:52.000 --> 01:34:54.000
I really miss you guys.

1496
01:34:56.000 --> 01:34:57.999
You guys really do look like best friends.

1497
01:34:58.000 --> 01:34:59.000
What do you mean?

1498
01:35:08.000 --> 01:35:09.999
You should tell him.

1499
01:35:10.000 --> 01:35:11.000
He can handle it.

1500
01:35:13.000 --> 01:35:14.000
Yeah. I know.

1501
01:35:16.000 --> 01:35:18.000
Um...

1502
01:35:21.000 --> 01:35:22.999
When she was inhabiting you.

1503
01:35:23.000 --> 01:35:25.000
on the rooftop.

1504
01:35:26.000 --> 01:35:27.999
she kissed me..

1505
01:35:28.000 --> 01:35:29.999
And I kissed her back..

1506
01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:31.999
Because I thought it was you.

1507
01:35:32.000 --> 01:35:33.000
but I didn't know.

1508
01:35:33.001 --> 01:35:35.000
And I'm really sorry.

1509
01:35:36.000 --> 01:35:38.000
I just thought you should know.

1510
01:35:40.000 --> 01:35:42.000
Thanks for telling me.

1511
01:35:45.000 --> 01:35:46.000
I mean. it's not like.

1512
01:35:46.001 --> 01:35:48.000
I remember anything anyway. so...

1513
01:35:49.000 --> 01:35:50.000
Really?

1514
01:35:50.000 --> 01:35:51.000
Yeah.

1515
01:35:51.000 --> 01:35:52.000
It was weird.

1516
01:35:52.001 --> 01:35:53.999
It was like one second I
was sitting in my desk..

1517
01:35:54.000 --> 01:35:55.999
And the next second I
was lying on the street.

1518
01:35:56.000 --> 01:35:58.000
I don't know. like. a
light switch went off.

1519
01:36:00.000 --> 01:36:01.000
What?

1520
01:36:01.001 --> 01:36:03.000
So you don't remember anything?

1521
01:36:04.000 --> 01:36:05.999
No. why?

1522
01:36:06.000 --> 01:36:08.999
Metzger said. he remembered
thinking about someone named Sara.

1523
01:36:09.000 --> 01:36:12.000
but what you're saying is that
you don't remember anything at all.

1524
01:36:13.000 --> 01:36:15.999
I mean. yeah. it was instantaneous.

1525
01:36:16.000 --> 01:36:18.000
That's what made it so scary.

1526
01:36:19.000 --> 01:36:21.000
He lied to me.

1527
01:36:23.000 --> 01:36:24.999
I heard you call a leshy.

1528
01:36:25.000 --> 01:36:26.000
Yeah. her name's Jean Grey.

1529
01:36:26.001 --> 01:36:28.999
I need some help determining
the size of some potatoes.

1530
01:36:29.000 --> 01:36:30.999
- Potatoes?
- I think that's Black Widow.

1531
01:36:31.000 --> 01:36:32.999
I think Metzger lied to me about a name.

1532
01:36:33.000 --> 01:36:34.999
Can you see if there's a
connection between Jean

1533
01:36:35.000 --> 01:36:36.999
and someone named Sara?

1534
01:36:37.000 --> 01:36:38.000
Hmm.

1535
01:36:38.001 --> 01:36:40.000
This potato sound meager.

1536
01:36:41.000 --> 01:36:42.999
Oh. well. that really is your office.

1537
01:36:43.000 --> 01:36:44.999
Well. well. well.

1538
01:36:45.000 --> 01:36:46.999
Internet. government records.

1539
01:36:47.000 --> 01:36:48.999
and a lot of data related to Jean Grey

1540
01:36:49.000 --> 01:36:51.999
has been scrubbed by Damage Control.

1541
01:36:52.000 --> 01:36:53.999
They know about what?

1542
01:36:54.000 --> 01:36:55.000
Her sister.

1543
01:36:55.001 --> 01:36:57.000
Wait. Jean has a sister?

1544
01:36:59.000 --> 01:37:00.999
Yeah. Sara Grey.

1545
01:37:01.000 --> 01:37:02.000
Also with telepath.

1546
01:37:02.001 --> 01:37:03.999
Damage Control took her into custody

1547
01:37:04.000 --> 01:37:05.999
for study and observation.

1548
01:37:06.000 --> 01:37:07.000
Wow.

1549
01:37:07.001 --> 01:37:08.999
You probably can guess
what they meant by that.

1550
01:37:09.000 --> 01:37:10.999
Experimentation and other
human rights violations.

1551
01:37:11.000 --> 01:37:12.000
Yes. exactly.

1552
01:37:12.000 --> 01:37:13.000
Wait. who are you?

1553
01:37:13.000 --> 01:37:14.000
Hi.

1554
01:37:14.000 --> 01:37:15.000
Ned Leeds. Big fan.

1555
01:37:15.000 --> 01:37:16.000
Hi.

1556
01:37:16.001 --> 01:37:17.999
Oh. I'm sorry.

1557
01:37:18.000 --> 01:37:21.000
I'm just so happy that
this person has friends.

1558
01:37:23.000 --> 01:37:24.000
Thanks.

1559
01:37:24.001 --> 01:37:25.999
I owe you one.

1560
01:37:26.000 --> 01:37:27.999
Good luck. Spider-Man.

1561
01:37:28.000 --> 01:37:29.000
Bye.

1562
01:37:29.000 --> 01:37:30.000
She was just looking for her sister.

1563
01:37:30.001 --> 01:37:31.999
and I handed it to the people who took her.

1564
01:37:32.000 --> 01:37:33.999
I gotta go.

1565
01:37:34.000 --> 01:37:35.999
Peter.

1566
01:37:36.000 --> 01:37:38.999
Just be careful. all right?

1567
01:37:39.000 --> 01:37:42.000
Oh. well.

1568
01:37:45.000 --> 01:37:48.000
Spider-Man's name is Peter.

1569
01:38:00.000 --> 01:38:04.000
Jean. who do you want to be?

1570
01:38:05.000 --> 01:38:07.999
Her. in the jacket.

1571
01:38:08.000 --> 01:38:09.999
She's too far.

1572
01:38:10.000 --> 01:38:11.999
You're gonna have to hop.

1573
01:38:12.000 --> 01:38:13.000
Hop?

1574
01:38:13.001 --> 01:38:14.999
First. pick something close.

1575
01:38:15.000 --> 01:38:17.000
And then...

1576
01:38:30.000 --> 01:38:31.999
The hop has a limit.

1577
01:38:32.000 --> 01:38:35.999
But you can string them
together and go as far as you want.

1578
01:38:36.000 --> 01:38:37.999
And when you let go...

1579
01:38:38.000 --> 01:38:40.999
You're back where you started.

1580
01:38:41.000 --> 01:38:43.999
Can you do that to
everyone in this park at once?

1581
01:38:44.000 --> 01:38:45.999
Well. yeah. maybe one day.

1582
01:38:46.000 --> 01:38:48.999
If you get really good.

1583
01:38:49.000 --> 01:38:51.000
No.

1584
01:39:01.000 --> 01:39:05.999
Now could she just send us away?

1585
01:39:06.000 --> 01:39:08.999
She wasn't really a mom.

1586
01:39:09.000 --> 01:39:10.999
Not like that. anyway.

1587
01:39:11.000 --> 01:39:12.000
She was.

1588
01:39:12.000 --> 01:39:13.000
Before we changed.

1589
01:39:13.001 --> 01:39:14.999
And if that's all it takes for
you to stop being a mom.

1590
01:39:15.000 --> 01:39:16.999
then you're not a mom.

1591
01:39:17.000 --> 01:39:19.999
What would you do if
you had daughters like us?

1592
01:39:20.000 --> 01:39:22.000
I'd love them.

1593
01:39:24.000 --> 01:39:25.999
Especially the redhead one.

1594
01:39:26.000 --> 01:39:27.999
Shut up.

1595
01:39:28.000 --> 01:39:31.000
We have each other.

1596
01:39:34.000 --> 01:39:36.999
And give me an ice cream.

1597
01:39:37.000 --> 01:39:40.000
One mint chip. one chocolate?

1598
01:40:13.000 --> 01:40:15.000
Sara?!

1599
01:40:20.000 --> 01:40:24.000
I'm sorry. Jean.
I have to keep you safe.

1600
01:41:07.000 --> 01:41:10.999
Subject is awake. heart rate is 94 BPM.

1601
01:41:11.000 --> 01:41:12.999
Jean. that's not going to work anymore.

1602
01:41:13.000 --> 01:41:15.000
Thanks to Spider-Man.

1603
01:41:20.000 --> 01:41:22.000
Jean...

1604
01:41:31.000 --> 01:41:32.999
I need you to breathe.

1605
01:41:33.000 --> 01:41:34.999
I need you to look at me and breathe.

1606
01:41:35.000 --> 01:41:37.000
You're safe. Breathe.

1607
01:41:39.000 --> 01:41:40.999
Where is she?

1608
01:41:41.000 --> 01:41:46.999
Like your sister. you've been blessed with a power that
has the potential to do tremendous good in the world..

1609
01:41:47.000 --> 01:41:48.999
Or tremendous damage.

1610
01:41:49.000 --> 01:41:52.999
The power like yours in the hands
of a child is an impossible burden.

1611
01:41:53.000 --> 01:41:54.999
But imagine...

1612
01:41:55.000 --> 01:42:00.999
If that power was placed in the hands of
people who actually know what to do with it.

1613
01:42:01.000 --> 01:42:09.000
Where is my sister?

1614
01:42:11.000 --> 01:42:14.999
You're going to change the world. Jean.

1615
01:42:15.000 --> 01:42:16.999
Hey!

1616
01:42:17.000 --> 01:42:18.999
Hey!

1617
01:42:19.000 --> 01:42:21.000
No!

1618
01:42:42.000 --> 01:42:43.999
I know where you are
and what are you doing.

1619
01:42:44.000 --> 01:42:45.000
Oh. yeah. how's that?

1620
01:42:45.001 --> 01:42:47.000
I Got eyes everywhere. kid.

1621
01:42:49.000 --> 01:42:51.499
Look. Frank.
Damage Control kidnapped Gene's sister.

1622
01:42:51.500 --> 01:42:52.999
Jean was just trying to find her.

1623
01:42:53.000 --> 01:42:54.999
We were wrong about everything.

1624
01:42:55.000 --> 01:42:56.999
Sentimental horseshit.

1625
01:42:57.000 --> 01:42:58.999
You've seen what she can do. what she's
capable of. what you're gonna let her loose?

1626
01:42:59.000 --> 01:43:00.999
Is that what you're going to do?

1627
01:43:01.000 --> 01:43:04.999
Tell you right now you do that.
I'll handle it my way.

1628
01:43:05.000 --> 01:43:06.999
Frank. listen to me. You just..

1629
01:43:07.000 --> 01:43:09.000
Frank!

1630
01:43:21.000 --> 01:43:22.999
Distance check?

1631
01:43:23.000 --> 01:43:24.999
Forty-foot clearance.

1632
01:43:25.000 --> 01:43:27.000
Locking down the room.

1633
01:43:31.000 --> 01:43:33.000
Disengage inhibitor.

1634
01:43:37.000 --> 01:43:39.000
Jean. your powers are
now fully operational.

1635
01:43:47.000 --> 01:43:50.999
As you can tell. you're
beyond your jump radius.

1636
01:43:51.000 --> 01:43:54.999
Tell me what V-Max is.

1637
01:43:55.000 --> 01:43:58.999
You're the second person
to ask me about that.

1638
01:43:59.000 --> 01:44:00.999
I have no idea what that means.

1639
01:44:01.000 --> 01:44:02.999
She sent me a message.

1640
01:44:03.000 --> 01:44:04.999
She was trying to help me find her.

1641
01:44:05.000 --> 01:44:08.999
She communicated with you
telepathically across all that distance?

1642
01:44:09.000 --> 01:44:12.999
We did register a huge
spike in that session.

1643
01:44:13.000 --> 01:44:14.999
Fascinating.

1644
01:44:15.000 --> 01:44:17.000
What does it mean?

1645
01:44:19.000 --> 01:44:20.999
I don't know.

1646
01:44:21.000 --> 01:44:23.000
Let's begin.

1647
01:44:31.000 --> 01:44:32.999
Our work with Sara is central on two areas.

1648
01:44:33.000 --> 01:44:38.000
Identifying the source of her power and
identifying her path towards copying you.

1649
01:44:39.000 --> 01:44:41.999
If we could find a way to record
a telepathic brain during a jump.

1650
01:44:42.000 --> 01:44:47.000
then perhaps we could replicate those
pathways in the mind of our choosing.

1651
01:44:48.000 --> 01:44:51.000
This instrument is your sister's legacy.

1652
01:44:52.000 --> 01:44:56.000
We built this together
over many months of trial.

1653
01:44:57.000 --> 01:44:59.000
I hope you and I can honor her sacrifice.

1654
01:45:02.000 --> 01:45:04.000
What are you talking about?

1655
01:45:05.000 --> 01:45:07.000
Trigger the first jump.

1656
01:45:10.000 --> 01:45:12.999
Tell me what V-max is.

1657
01:45:13.000 --> 01:45:17.000
I know that's where you're hiding her.

1658
01:45:29.000 --> 01:45:32.999
She's jumping.

1659
01:45:33.000 --> 01:45:34.999
Copy.

1660
01:45:35.000 --> 01:45:36.999
We're in full lockdown.

1661
01:45:37.000 --> 01:45:38.999
The process has commenced.

1662
01:45:39.000 --> 01:45:40.999
What process?

1663
01:45:41.000 --> 01:45:44.999
Hey. whoa. that's a pretty
serious look there. dude.

1664
01:45:45.000 --> 01:45:46.999
Hey. whoa. what the hell. man?

1665
01:45:47.000 --> 01:45:48.999
Come on. I'm a friend of Damage Control.

1666
01:45:49.000 --> 01:45:50.999
What are you doing?

1667
01:45:51.000 --> 01:45:52.999
Huh.

1668
01:45:53.000 --> 01:45:54.999
It's going to be like that. You want to go.

1669
01:45:55.000 --> 01:45:58.999
All right. All right. just give me a sec.

1670
01:45:59.000 --> 01:46:00.999
Give me a sec.

1671
01:46:01.000 --> 01:46:02.999
I'm not in high school anymore.

1672
01:46:03.000 --> 01:46:04.999
Oh... Do you stretch?
Are you a big stretcher?

1673
01:46:05.000 --> 01:46:06.999
You should do it in your line of work.

1674
01:46:07.000 --> 01:46:08.999
What about you? You guys stretch?

1675
01:46:09.000 --> 01:46:10.999
It's so good for you.

1676
01:46:11.000 --> 01:46:13.000
You ready?

1677
01:46:23.000 --> 01:46:24.000
Watch your head!

1678
01:46:43.000 --> 01:46:44.000
Where is Jean Gray?

1679
01:46:46.000 --> 01:46:47.000
It's jump 26.

1680
01:46:47.000 --> 01:46:48.000
Recording looks good.

1681
01:46:49.000 --> 01:46:50.000
Excuse me. sir.

1682
01:46:51.000 --> 01:46:52.000
We have an intruder.

1683
01:46:45.000 --> 01:46:47.000
Oh.

1684
01:46:57.000 --> 01:46:58.999
You're right.

1685
01:46:59.000 --> 01:47:00.999
She's much stronger than her sister.

1686
01:47:01.000 --> 01:47:02.999
Increase the frequency.

1687
01:47:03.000 --> 01:47:05.000
You're doing very well. Jean.

1688
01:47:55.000 --> 01:47:57.000
Jean.

1689
01:47:59.000 --> 01:48:01.000
Jean. can you hear me?

1690
01:48:06.000 --> 01:48:07.000
Jean?

1691
01:48:13.000 --> 01:48:14.000
You're a murderer.

1692
01:48:16.000 --> 01:48:18.999
Her frequencies are evolving.

1693
01:48:19.000 --> 01:48:20.000
This doesn't make sense.

1694
01:48:22.000 --> 01:48:24.999
The last thing my sister saw was this room.

1695
01:48:25.000 --> 01:48:27.999
A brainwaves is somehow
affecting the objects around her.

1696
01:48:28.000 --> 01:48:30.999
- Shut it down.
- I'm trying. sir.

1697
01:48:31.000 --> 01:48:32.240
What do you mean you're trying?

1698
01:48:33.000 --> 01:48:37.000
The last thing my sister
saw was this God damn room!

1699
01:48:38.000 --> 01:48:40.000
- Shut it down!
- I can't. sir.

1700
01:48:44.000 --> 01:48:46.000
I can't let you do that. Bill.

1701
01:48:50.000 --> 01:48:56.000
The only hand that wields
this power.. Are mine.

1702
01:51:07.000 --> 01:51:10.000
What do you want?

1703
01:51:14.000 --> 01:51:17.000
Jean. I'm here to help you.

1704
01:51:18.000 --> 01:51:19.999
You put me here.

1705
01:51:20.000 --> 01:51:24.000
I know. and I'm sorry about Sara.
and I'm sorry that I got it so wrong.

1706
01:51:27.000 --> 01:51:31.000
If you came here to save the helpless
girl from Damage Control. you're too late.

1707
01:51:32.000 --> 01:51:33.999
They're the ones who need saving.

1708
01:51:34.000 --> 01:51:37.000
And now. so do you.

1709
01:51:39.000 --> 01:51:41.000
Here we go.

1710
01:51:55.000 --> 01:51:57.000
God. that's cool.

1711
01:52:04.000 --> 01:52:07.000
I'm here to help you.

1712
01:52:18.000 --> 01:52:20.000
Jean. Jean. please!

1713
01:52:34.000 --> 01:52:36.000
Come on. come on. come on!

1714
01:52:37.000 --> 01:52:39.000
What?

1715
01:52:58.000 --> 01:53:05.000
Isn't it funny how your friends from Damage
Control developed a special weapon just for you?

1716
01:53:06.000 --> 01:53:08.999
They've got a whole task force ready.

1717
01:53:09.000 --> 01:53:12.000
Just in case you ever get out of line.

1718
01:53:15.000 --> 01:53:18.000
People are monsters.

1719
01:53:21.000 --> 01:53:25.000
You shouldn't trust them
any more than they trust you.

1720
01:53:37.000 --> 01:53:38.999
I'm a little busy. Frank!

1721
01:53:39.000 --> 01:53:40.999
We got a problem. kid.

1722
01:53:41.000 --> 01:53:43.999
She got a hold of everyone
within a kilometer of the island.

1723
01:53:44.000 --> 01:53:46.000
Wait. what?

1724
01:53:51.000 --> 01:53:53.999
Look. if you're going to do
something. you gotta do it now.

1725
01:53:54.000 --> 01:53:56.000
I'm trying!!

1726
01:54:20.000 --> 01:54:23.000
Kid! Shit!

1727
01:54:57.000 --> 01:55:00.000
My sister died in this room.

1728
01:55:01.000 --> 01:55:03.000
Surrounded by these men.

1729
01:55:04.000 --> 01:55:07.999
And her only crime
was that she was special.

1730
01:55:08.000 --> 01:55:10.999
Just like you.

1731
01:55:11.000 --> 01:55:14.000
Just like me.

1732
01:55:15.000 --> 01:55:19.000
People like us don't
get to live a normal life.

1733
01:55:21.000 --> 01:55:25.999
We don't get to have friends or family.

1734
01:55:26.000 --> 01:55:29.000
Those people are gone.

1735
01:55:30.000 --> 01:55:33.000
That life is over.

1736
01:55:58.000 --> 01:56:01.000
So why don't you just
be honest with yourself?

1737
01:56:04.000 --> 01:56:06.999
Are you Peter Parker?

1738
01:56:07.000 --> 01:56:10.000
Or are you Spider-Man?

1739
01:56:42.000 --> 01:56:43.000
I'm both.

1740
01:58:27.000 --> 01:58:29.999
Jane. please.

1741
01:58:30.000 --> 01:58:32.000
This will make you right.

1742
01:58:34.000 --> 01:58:35.999
Come on. you're not a killer. Jean.

1743
01:58:36.000 --> 01:58:38.999
You have no idea what I am.

1744
01:58:39.000 --> 01:58:42.000
I know that you loved your sister.

1745
01:58:44.000 --> 01:58:46.999
And I know that losing her
felt like you'd lost everything.

1746
01:58:47.000 --> 01:58:51.000
If you come any closer.
he dies! They all do!

1747
01:59:08.000 --> 01:59:10.000
You know this won't
bring her back. right. Jean?

1748
01:59:28.000 --> 01:59:31.999
Don't be so sure I
can't get into your mind.

1749
01:59:32.000 --> 01:59:35.000
I'm a lot more powerful since I last tried.

1750
01:59:44.000 --> 01:59:46.000
Go ahead.

1751
01:59:54.000 --> 01:59:56.000
Hey.

1752
01:59:57.000 --> 01:59:59.000
Hey.

1753
02:00:00.000 --> 02:00:04.000
You think you don't have to listen
to me. now you've got powers?

1754
02:00:09.000 --> 02:00:13.999
You know. this whole
thing. can get really scary.

1755
02:00:14.000 --> 02:00:17.000
You know that?

1756
02:00:34.000 --> 02:00:37.000
It's already pretty scary.

1757
02:00:38.000 --> 02:00:41.999
And things can change very quickly.

1758
02:00:42.000 --> 02:00:44.999
In ways that we can't
even imagine right now.

1759
02:00:45.000 --> 02:00:47.000
I know.

1760
02:00:49.000 --> 02:00:52.000
I don't think you do now.

1761
02:00:53.000 --> 02:00:55.000
What do you mean?

1762
02:00:57.000 --> 02:01:00.000
You're a really special person.

1763
02:01:01.000 --> 02:01:04.999
And I would hope that that will always
make you feel really great about yourself.

1764
02:01:05.000 --> 02:01:07.999
But I know sometimes it doesn't.

1765
02:01:08.000 --> 02:01:12.000
Sometimes it'll be really lonely.

1766
02:01:14.000 --> 02:01:19.000
And sometimes. because you're special.

1767
02:01:20.000 --> 02:01:26.000
people can do dark.
monstrous things to you.

1768
02:01:27.000 --> 02:01:31.999
But this is what I want you to know.

1769
02:01:32.000 --> 02:01:34.999
You're beautiful..

1770
02:01:35.000 --> 02:01:37.999
And the people who love you. we love you..

1771
02:01:38.000 --> 02:01:41.999
Not because you're special.
we love you. because you're you.

1772
02:01:42.000 --> 02:01:45.999
I want you to remember that.

1773
02:01:46.000 --> 02:01:50.999
Even when you feel
like you're totally alone.

1774
02:01:51.000 --> 02:01:55.999
That's your deepest responsibility.

1775
02:01:56.000 --> 02:02:01.000
Never forget that. no matter
how powerful you become.

1776
02:02:15.000 --> 02:02:18.000
Hey.

1777
02:02:32.000 --> 02:02:34.000
I'm sorry about your. sister.

1778
02:02:38.000 --> 02:02:42.999
I'm sorry about your aunt.

1779
02:02:43.000 --> 02:02:48.000
Yeah. you would've loved her.

1780
02:02:49.000 --> 02:02:53.999
Just because we've lost someone..

1781
02:02:54.000 --> 02:02:57.999
It doesn't mean we have to do this alone.

1782
02:02:58.000 --> 02:03:05.999
I mean. we can't. Trust
me. I've been trying.

1783
02:03:06.000 --> 02:03:11.999
It doesn't work.

1784
02:03:12.000 --> 02:03:17.000
Even if that's true.

1785
02:03:18.000 --> 02:03:22.999
I have no one.

1786
02:03:23.000 --> 02:03:29.000
You have me.

1787
02:03:50.000 --> 02:03:51.000
No.

1788
02:04:09.000 --> 02:04:11.999
You hurt?

1789
02:04:12.000 --> 02:04:15.000
No. I'm fine.

1790
02:04:20.000 --> 02:04:21.999
- Peter.
- I'm okay. I'm okay. I'm okay.

1791
02:04:22.000 --> 02:04:26.999
Peter. No. no. no.

1792
02:04:27.000 --> 02:04:31.999
No. no. no. no. Peter.

1793
02:04:32.000 --> 02:04:34.999
You gotta get out of here.

1794
02:04:35.000 --> 02:04:38.000
No. please just stay with me.
Come on. hold on. come on. Please!

1795
02:04:39.000 --> 02:04:43.999
You're gonna be okay.
Just go.

1796
02:04:44.000 --> 02:04:49.000
Yeah. look at me.

1797
02:05:04.000 --> 02:05:05.999
Shock today.

1798
02:05:06.000 --> 02:05:09.999
As spider man arrived to Bellevue
Hospital with a bullet wound..

1799
02:05:10.000 --> 02:05:12.999
Seemingly at that death's door.

1800
02:05:13.000 --> 02:05:21.000
The reclusive crime fighter is in critical condition
as the city's top medical experts work to save him.

1801
02:05:22.000 --> 02:05:26.999
Tonight. all eyes are on Spider-Man.

1802
02:05:27.000 --> 02:05:34.999
The hero who saved New York so many times is
now in the hands of its best and brightest.

1803
02:05:35.000 --> 02:05:42.000
And the people of New
York hold their breath.

1804
02:06:44.000 --> 02:06:48.999
Frank.

1805
02:06:49.000 --> 02:06:51.999
Where am I?

1806
02:06:52.000 --> 02:06:54.999
- No. no. no. no. no. Wear your mask.
- Where's my mask?

1807
02:06:55.000 --> 02:06:57.999
Don't worry. I've got you covered.
You're good.

1808
02:06:58.000 --> 02:06:59.999
Where's Jean? Is she okay?

1809
02:07:00.000 --> 02:07:02.999
- Yeah. she's okay.
- Where is she?

1810
02:07:03.000 --> 02:07:06.999
I think she just left.

1811
02:07:07.000 --> 02:07:13.999
She was using her magic
voodoo shit to keep you alive.

1812
02:07:14.000 --> 02:07:20.999
Yeah. she's all right.

1813
02:07:21.000 --> 02:07:27.999
I'm sorry.

1814
02:07:28.000 --> 02:07:31.999
- No. Frank. it's okay.
- I'm sorry for what I did.

1815
02:07:32.000 --> 02:07:36.999
I know it's a lot of things. but it
sure as shit wasn't okay. all right?

1816
02:07:37.000 --> 02:07:39.999
I've seen..

1817
02:07:40.000 --> 02:07:46.999
I've seen real bravery. kid. in my day.

1818
02:07:47.000 --> 02:07:52.999
But that... that was something else.

1819
02:07:53.000 --> 02:07:59.999
- You crying. Frank?
- No. I ain't crying!

1820
02:08:00.000 --> 02:08:06.999
No. you're looking the exactly
the way I thought you would.

1821
02:08:07.000 --> 02:08:10.999
A nice kid.

1822
02:08:11.000 --> 02:08:13.999
I've never had a friend like that.

1823
02:08:14.000 --> 02:08:22.000
Are we friends now?

1824
02:08:23.000 --> 02:08:24.999
I can't believe I just saw you cry.

1825
02:08:25.000 --> 02:08:29.999
I didn't cry. What are you talking about?

1826
02:08:30.000 --> 02:08:31.999
Oh. yeah.

1827
02:08:32.000 --> 02:08:34.999
They've been doing it all night.
they've been here since you walked in.

1828
02:08:35.000 --> 02:08:39.999
Just take a look.

1829
02:08:40.000 --> 02:08:47.999
Yo. kid.

1830
02:08:48.000 --> 02:08:54.000
When you came in they had to cut through the suit.
but when you're ready to split. I got a plan.

1831
02:09:16.000 --> 02:09:19.000
Hey. it's Spider-Man!

1832
02:11:49.000 --> 02:11:50.999
I've. uh...

1833
02:11:51.000 --> 02:11:57.999
Been thinking a lot about what you said.

1834
02:11:58.000 --> 02:12:01.999
And you'd be happy to
know that I've decided I'm not..

1835
02:12:02.000 --> 02:12:08.999
I'm not going to do this alone anymore.

1836
02:12:09.000 --> 02:12:17.000
I miss you. May.

1837
02:12:23.000 --> 02:12:28.000
I mean. I still got a little pain in my back. but I could
probably get back out there if you need me for anything.

1838
02:12:29.000 --> 02:12:30.999
What I need you to do is rest.

1839
02:12:31.000 --> 02:12:32.000
I know. I know.

1840
02:12:32.000 --> 02:12:33.000
Well. come on. you gotta give me something.

1841
02:12:33.001 --> 02:12:34.999
I mean. how's the investigation going?

1842
02:12:35.000 --> 02:12:36.999
Well. that's good.

1843
02:12:37.000 --> 02:12:38.000
Don't you see?

1844
02:12:38.001 --> 02:12:42.999
But your friend. Black Widow. she's been
helping us get through all the records.

1845
02:12:43.000 --> 02:12:45.999
Damage Control tried to have scrubbed.

1846
02:12:46.000 --> 02:12:47.999
Had me dropped by her office the other day.

1847
02:12:48.000 --> 02:12:49.999
And how was that?

1848
02:12:50.000 --> 02:12:53.999
Well. my skin feels amazing.

1849
02:12:54.000 --> 02:12:55.000
Attention. all units.

1850
02:12:55.001 --> 02:12:56.999
We have a confirmed
bank robbery in progress.

1851
02:12:57.000 --> 02:12:59.999
Hey. are you getting this?

1852
02:13:00.000 --> 02:13:01.000
Yeah. I'm on it.

1853
02:13:01.000 --> 02:13:02.000
Hey. it's not that far from me.

1854
02:13:02.001 --> 02:13:03.999
I could probably meet you down there.

1855
02:13:04.000 --> 02:13:06.999
No. we can handle a robbery.

1856
02:13:07.000 --> 02:13:10.999
Just try to take care of yourself.

1857
02:13:11.000 --> 02:13:13.999
Okay.

1858
02:13:14.000 --> 02:13:15.999
You too.

1859
02:13:16.000 --> 02:13:18.999
Say hello to E.J. and Marley for me.

1860
02:13:19.000 --> 02:13:21.999
Okay.

1861
02:13:22.000 --> 02:13:25.000
Spider-Man says hello.

1862
02:13:59.000 --> 02:14:00.999
